From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Connolly <david@connol.ly>
Date: Thu, 06 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] cpu/intel/model_206ax: add configurable
 energy-performance bias

The Energy-Performance Bias hint (IA32_ENERGY_PERF_BIAS, MSR 0x1b0)
is currently hardcoded to ENERGY_POLICY_NORMAL (value 6).  This
tells the hardware power management unit to tolerate moderate
performance loss in exchange for energy savings, affecting how
aggressively the CPU transitions between P-states and enters
opportunistic turbo.

On desktop systems targeting maximum turbo stability, a value of 0
(ENERGY_POLICY_PERFORMANCE) makes the hardware P-state controller
react faster to load changes, reducing time spent at intermediate
voltage/frequency points during ramp-up.  This eliminates a class
of transient undervolt where the CPU begins executing at a high
ratio before the voltage request has fully propagated.

EPB value mapping (Intel SDM):
  0  = performance     (fastest P-state transitions)
  4  = balance-performance
  6  = normal           (current default)
  8  = balance-power
  15 = power save       (most aggressive power savings)

Add a Kconfig int ENERGY_PERF_BIAS (range 0-15, default 6) to make
this configurable without changing the default behaviour.

Note: Linux may override this value at boot via the intel_epb driver
or the x86_energy_perf_policy tool, but the firmware setting
establishes the initial policy for early boot and for operating
systems that do not reprogram the MSR.

Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000012
Signed-off-by: David Connolly <david@connol.ly>
---
 src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/Kconfig            | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/model_206ax_init.c |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/Kconfig b/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/Kconfig
index 3333333333..4444444444 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/Kconfig
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/Kconfig
@@ -54,4 +54,22 @@ config PKG_CSTATE_LIMIT
 
 	  Use 0 for overclocked desktops, 7 for laptops/servers.
 
+config ENERGY_PERF_BIAS
+	int "Energy-Performance Bias (EPB) hint value"
+	default 6
+	range 0 15
+	help
+	  Initial value for IA32_ENERGY_PERF_BIAS (MSR 0x1b0).
+	  Controls how aggressively the hardware trades performance
+	  for power savings in P-state and turbo decisions.
+
+	    0  = performance (fastest transitions, no power saving)
+	    4  = balance-performance
+	    6  = normal (default)
+	    8  = balance-power
+	    15 = power save (most aggressive saving)
+
+	  Use 0 for overclocked desktops.  Note that Linux may
+	  override this via the intel_epb driver at OS boot.
+
 endif # CPU_INTEL_MODEL_206AX
diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/model_206ax_init.c b/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/model_206ax_init.c
index 5555555555..6666666666 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/model_206ax_init.c
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/model_206ax_init.c
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@ static void model_206ax_init(struct device *cpu)
 	configure_dca_cap();
 
 	/* Set energy policy */
-	set_energy_perf_bias(ENERGY_POLICY_NORMAL);
+	set_energy_perf_bias(CONFIG_ENERGY_PERF_BIAS);
 
 	/* Set Max Ratio */
 	set_max_ratio();
